# TestBuddy — Architecture & Conventions

## Product

Browser extension + platform that records a session and produces either a **bug report** or **test cases**. AI layer *writes* (humanizes steps, expected results, test-case drafts) — it does **not** do visual bug detection.

Full product spec: `PROJECT_SPEC.md`. Build only the current phase; do not skip ahead.

## Stack (fixed)

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Extension | TypeScript + React, Manifest V3, `webextension-polyfill` |
| Backend | Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL (`pg`), JWT (jsonwebtoken), bcrypt |
| AI service | Python 3.11+, FastAPI, LLM API — **internal only**, never browser-facing |
| Frontend | React + TypeScript, Vite, TanStack Query, Tailwind CSS |
| Files | S3-compatible object storage (not Postgres) |
| Integrations | Jira REST v3, Azure DevOps REST, Apache POI |

## Repo layout

```
extension/   backend/   ai-service/   frontend/
```

## Architecture

```
Extension ──JWT/REST──► Node Backend ──► PostgreSQL
                            │
                            ├──► AI service (internal)
                            ├──► Object storage
                            └──► Jira / Azure DevOps

Frontend dashboard ──► same Node Backend
```

## Shared domain shapes

Mirror these in the Node backend (DB rows / mappers) and as TypeScript interfaces (frontend + extension):

- `User` — roles: ADMIN | TESTER | DEVELOPER | MANAGER
- `Project` — optional jiraProjectKey, adoOrgUrl, adoProject
- `Cycle` — projectId, name, isDefault (dropdown defaults to Cycle 1)
- `Step` — order, actionType, elementLabel, selector, valueEntered (mask passwords as `••••`), pageUrl, description, expectedResult?
- `Annotation` / `Attachment` — screenshot/video metadata
- `Bug` — priority, severity, assignee/reporter/cycle/project, status, steps, attachments, externalRefs
- `TestCase` — type POSITIVE|NEGATIVE, status AI_DRAFT|VERIFIED|REJECTED|UPLOADED, generatedByAi

## API surface (owned by backend)

Auth, users, projects, cycles, bugs CRUD, testcases CRUD + generate/verify/bulk-upload, exports, Jira/ADO push. AI routes (`/ai/...`) live **only** on the Python service and are called server-to-server.

## Privacy

Never store raw password / sensitive autocomplete values — use `••••` and blur those regions in screenshots by default.

## Phase discipline

Ask before architectural decisions not covered by `PROJECT_SPEC.md`. Do not implement recording, AI generation, or integrations until their phase.
